  Datapipe is an open-source streaming ETL framework, built in Rust with Python bindings, designed for data engineers. It allows for[0m[2m the efficient movement of billions of events daily between platforms like Kafka, S3, Postgres, and ClickHouse, eliminating the need for custom connector development. The framework offers over 40 pre-built source/sink connectors, guarantees exactly-once delivery[0m[2m through two-phase commit, and features a declarative transformation DSL that compiles to optimized Rust. It is ideal for mid-sized data teams (5-50 engineers) managing high event volumes (1B+ events/day) who seek[0m[2m to consolidate disparate data pipelines. Installation is straightforward via `pip install datapipe-core`, with an option for `datapipe[all]` for the complete connector suite.
     
